    {
      "heading": "Arithmetic with complex numbers",
      "questions": [
        {
          "q": "Let $z_1=4-2i$ and $z_2=-3+i$. Find $z_1+z_2$ and $z_1z_2$.",
          "answer": "$z_1+z_2=(4-3)+(-2+1)i=1-i$. $z_1z_2=(4)(-3)-(-2)(1)+\\left[(4)(1)+(-2)(-3)\\right]i=-10+10i$."
        },
        {
          "q": "Find $(6+i)-(2-5i)$.",
          "answer": "$=4+6i$"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Complex roots of a quadratic",
      "questions": [
        {
          "q": "Solve $x^2+6x+13=0$.",
          "answer": "$\\Delta=6^2-4(1)(13)=36-52=-16<0$. By Theorem 1.1, $x=\\dfrac{-6\\pm\\sqrt{-16}}{2}=\\dfrac{-6\\pm4i}{2}=-3\\pm2i$."
        },
        {
          "q": "Solve $2x^2-4x+10=0$.",
          "answer": "$\\Delta=(-4)^2-4(2)(10)=16-80=-64<0$. $x=\\dfrac{4\\pm\\sqrt{-64}}{4}=\\dfrac{4\\pm8i}{4}=1\\pm2i$."
        },
        {
          "q": "Without solving it, explain how you know $x^2+2x+5=0$ has complex (not real) roots.",
          "answer": "Its discriminant is $\\Delta=2^2-4(1)(5)=4-20=-16<0$. A negative discriminant means the quadratic formula takes the square root of a negative number, giving a complex conjugate pair (Theorem 1.1) instead of real roots."
        },
        {
          "q": "Verify that $x=-3+2i$ is a root of $x^2+6x+13=0$ by direct substitution.",
          "answer": "$(-3+2i)^2=9-12i+4i^2=9-12i-4=5-12i$. And $6(-3+2i)=-18+12i$. Adding: $(5-12i)+(-18+12i)+13=0$. Yes, it checks out."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Modulus",
      "questions": [
        {
          "q": "Find $|z|$ for $z=-3+2i$ (one of the roots found above).",
          "answer": "$|z|=\\sqrt{(-3)^2+2^2}=\\sqrt{13}$."
        },
        {
          "q": "Find $|z|$ for $z=5-12i$.",
          "answer": "$|z|=\\sqrt{5^2+12^2}=\\sqrt{169}=13$."
        },
        {
          "q": "Explain why a conjugate pair $a\\pm bi$ always has the same modulus for both roots.",
          "answer": "$|a+bi|=\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}$ and $|a-bi|=\\sqrt{a^2+(-b)^2}=\\sqrt{a^2+b^2}$ \u2014 squaring $b$ or $-b$ gives the same result, so the two moduli are identical."
        }
      ]
